  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Kadsuralignan H may interact with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 through a series of target-mediated pathways. The compound targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and (+)-(5S,7R)-7-Ethoxy-12-Hydroxy-2-Oxo-20-Norabieta-1(10),8,11,13-Tetraene. These latter two compounds also direct their targets to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. The scores from the three paths are consistent, indicating a potential role for Kadsuralignan H in modulating the proteasome complex through its interaction with demethylase enzymes, which may influence the activity or stability of the regulatory subunit. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism involving the regulation of proteasome function via demethylase activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
